      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Key Price Drivers in Utah"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Pitch and Steepness: Roofs with a steep pitch (8/12 or higher) require extra safety equipment and labor, adding 10% to 20% to the bill."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Tear-Off and Layers: Removing multiple old layers of shingles or heavy cedar shakes increases labor and disposal fees."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Decking Replacement: Rotted or damaged plywood sheathing typically adds around $85 per sheet after initial allowances."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Snow and Ice Underlayment: Utah's heavy winter snow loads often require specialized high-grade ice-and-water shields in valleys and eaves.",
